{"causes": ["The rise of instrumental music in the Baroque period set the stage for the development of preludes.", "The influence of early keyboard music encouraged composers to create short, standalone pieces that could introduce larger works.", "The formalization of musical structures during the Classical era led to the establishment of the prelude as a recognized compositional form."], "effects": ["The prelude established a new standard for musical introductions, influencing the structure of later compositions.", "Subsequent musical forms, including the intermezzo and nocturne, were shaped by the stylistic innovations introduced in preludes.", "The concept of the prelude influenced the development of genres beyond classical music, including jazz and popular music."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "johann-sebastian-bach", "sourceName": "Johann Sebastian Bach", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "prelude", "targetName": "Prelude", "context": "Bach's preludes, such as those in the Well-Tempered Clavier, formalized the prelude structure in the early 18th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "classical-era", "sourceName": "Classical Era", "verb": "FRAMES", "targetSlug": "prelude", "targetName": "Prelude", "context": "The Classical era (1750-1820) provided a cultural backdrop that allowed the prelude to flourish as a musical form."}, {"sourceSlug": "frédéric-chopin", "sourceName": "Frédéric Chopin", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "prelude", "targetName": "Prelude", "context": "Chopin's preludes (1839) expanded the emotional depth and complexity of the prelude form, influencing later composers."}, {"sourceSlug": "concert-halls", "sourceName": "Concert Halls", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "prelude", "targetName": "Prelude", "context": "Preludes were commonly performed in concert halls throughout Europe during the Classical era."}, {"sourceSlug": "wolfgang-amadeus-mozart", "sourceName": "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart", "verb": "COLLABORATES_WITH", "targetSlug": "prelude", "ta